---
/* CraftiPlays / Lands of Magic project page.  URL: /portfolio/craftiplays
   Images go in public/portfolio/craftiplays/ */
import ProjectPage from '../../layouts/ProjectPage.astro';

// Building blocks for the part below the description
import FeatureImage from '../../components/project/FeatureImage.astro';
import BigSmall from '../../components/project/BigSmall.astro';
import Statement from '../../components/project/Statement.astro';
import UnevenPair from '../../components/project/UnevenPair.astro';
import MyPart from '../../components/project/MyPart.astro';
---

<ProjectPage
  pageTitle="Lands of Magic — Game Assets — Paulina Cywoniuk"
  pageDescription="Illustrated game assets for the mobile game 'Lands of Magic' by CraftiPlays."

  logo="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-logo.png"
  logoAlt="CraftiPlays logo"

  title={'Lands of Magic'}
  subtitle="Mobile Game Assets Design"

  headerImage="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-header.png"
  headerAlt="Colourful illustrated game assets for Lands of Magic"

  accent="var(--color-cyan)"
  accentText="var(--color-purple)"

  keywords={["Mobile Game", "Unity + Adobe Suite", "Team", "10 months"]}
>

  <p>
    In 2021 I was part of a team at CraftiPlays, who hired me as a graphic designer for
    their ongoing project — a mobile game called <em>Lands of Magic</em>. My role
    consisted of making illustrations of assets for the game that were consistent with
    the style of an asset pack they had already purchased before I joined the team.
  </p>
  <p>
    All designs I made for them are vectorised in Illustrator, so that the whole team
    can use them according to their needs. In <em>Lands of Magic</em>, the illustrations
    became more than just functional assets; they played a role in immersing players in
    a magical world where visuals enrich the storytelling and gameplay experience.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="sections">

    <FeatureImage
      src="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-2.jpg"
      alt="Illustrated cauldron and magical houses in seasonal versions"
      label="Assets"
      caption="[one-line caption, e.g. one building, three seasons]"
    />

    <BigSmall
      bigSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-trees-development.jpg"
      bigAlt="Illustrated magical plants and trees"
            bigAlt="Illustrated magical plants and trees"
      bigFit="contain"
            smallSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-gui-pack.jpg"
      smallAlt="Preview of the GUI asset pack The Stone, the style my illustrations had to match"
      smallHref="https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/2d/gui/gui-the-stone-116852"
      smallCredit="Asset pack: GUI The Stone (not my work)"
      heading="Matching an existing style"
    >
      Every asset had to fit the style of an asset pack the team had already bought.
    </BigSmall>

    <Statement>
      [One sentence about what makes a game asset feel magical.]
    </Statement>

    <UnevenPair
      aSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-4.jpg"
      aAlt="in game currency in it's natural environment plus loading bar UI"
      aCaption="In-game environment with currencies and loading bar UI."
      bSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/green-eye-process.jpg"
      bAlt="Process of designing the Green Eye event currency"
      bCaption="Process of designing the Green Eye event currency."
    />

    <MyPart
      heading="From sketch to vector"
      mainAlt="NEW: one asset in Illustrator, from sketch to final vector"
    >
      All assets are vectorised in Illustrator so the whole team can use them. [One sentence on your process.]
    </MyPart>

  </Fragment>

</ProjectPage>